{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-2-1","title":"Isaiah 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Isaiah prophesies the coming of Christ's kingdom. 6 Wickedness is the cause of God's forsaking. 10 He exhorts to fear, because of the powerful effects of God's majesty.</p>\n<p>saw. 1:1; 13:1; Am 1:1; Mic 1:1; 6:9; Hab 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-2","title":"Isaiah 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>And it shall. Mic 4:1-3 in the last. Ge 49:1; Nu 24:14; Job 19:25; Jer 23:20; 30:24; 48:47; 49:39 Eze 38:16; Da 2:28; 10:14; Ac 2:17; 2Ti 3:1; Heb 1:2; 2Pe 3:3 the mountain. 30:29; Ps 68:15,16; Da 2:35,45; Zec 8:3; Re 20:4; 21:10-27 established. or, prepared. and all. 11:10; 27:13; 49:6; 60:11,12; Ps 2:8; 22:27; 72:8,17-19; 86:9 Jer 3:17; Mal 3:12; Re 11:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-3","title":"Isaiah 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Come ye. Jer 31:6; 50:4,5; Zec 8:20-23 he will teach. De 6:1; Ps 25:8,9; Mt 7:24; Lu 11:28; Joh 7:17; Ac 10:33; Jas 1:25 for out. 51:4,5; Ps 110:2; Lu 24:47; Ac 1:8; 13:46-48; Ro 10:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-4","title":"Isaiah 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>And he. 11:3,4; 1Sa 2:10; Ps 82:8; 96:13; 110:6; Joh 16:8-11; Ac 17:31 Re 19:11 and they. 9:7; 11:6-9; Ps 46:9; Ho 2:18; Joe 3:10; Mic 4:3; Zec 9:10 pruning-hooks. or, scythes. neither. 60:17,18; Ps 72:3-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-5","title":"Isaiah 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>come ye. 3; 50:10,11; 60:1,19; Ps 89:15; Lu 1:79; Joh 12:35,36; Ro 13:12-14 Eph 5:8; 1Th 5:5,6; 1Jo 1:7; Re 21:23,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-6","title":"Isaiah 2:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Therefore. De 31:16,17; 2Ch 15:2; 24:20; La 5:20; Ro 11:1,2,20 from the east. or, more than the east. Nu 23:7 and are. 8:19; 47:12,13; Ex 22:18; Le 19:31; 20:6; De 18:10-14; 1Ch 10:13 and they. Ex 34:16; Nu 25:1,2; De 21:11-13; 1Ki 11:1,2; Ne 13:23; Ps 106:35 Jer 10:2 please themselves in. or, abound with, etc.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-7","title":"Isaiah 2:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>land. De 17:16,17; 1Ki 10:21-27; 2Ch 9:20-25; Jer 5:27,28; Jas 5:1-3 Re 18:3,11-17 their land is. 30:16; 31:1; De 17:16; 1Ki 4:26; 10:26; Ps 20:7; Ho 14:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-8","title":"Isaiah 2:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>is full. 57:5; 2Ch 27:2; 28:2-4,23-25; 33:3-7; Jer 2:28; 11:13; Eze 16:23-25 Ho 12:11; Ac 17:16 worship. 37:19; 44:15-20; De 4:28; Ps 115:4-8; Ho 8:6; 13:2; 14:3; Re 9:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-9","title":"Isaiah 2:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the mean. 5:15; Ps 49:2; Jer 5:4,5; Ro 3:23; Re 6:15-17 humbleth. 57:9; Col 2:18,23 therefore. 27:11; Jos 24:19; Jer 18:23; Mr 3:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-10","title":"Isaiah 2:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Enter. 19-21; 10:3; 42:22; Jud 6:1,2; Job 30:5,6; Ho 10:8; Lu 23:30 Re 6:15,16 for fear. 6:3-5; Job 31:23; 37:22-24; Ps 90:11; Jer 10:7,10; Lu 12:5 Re 15:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-11","title":"Isaiah 2:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>lofty. 17; 5:15,16; 13:11; 24:21; Job 40:10-12; Ps 18:27; Jer 50:31,32 Mal 4:1; Lu 18:14; 1Pe 5:5 and the Lord. 5:16; 12:4; Jer 9:24; 1Co 1:29-31; 2Co 10:17 in that day. 4:1; 11:10,11; 12:1,4; 24:21; 25:9; 26:1; 27:1,2,12,13; 28:5; 29:18 30:23; 52:6; Jer 30:7,8; Eze 38:14,19; 39:11,22; Ho 2:16,18,21 Joe 3:18; Am 9:11; Ob 1:8; Mic 4:6; 5:10; 7:11,12; Zep 3:11,16 Zec 9:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-12","title":"Isaiah 2:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>the day. 13:6,9; Jer 46:10; Eze 13:5; Am 5:18; Mal 4:5; 1Co 5:5; 1Th 5:2 upon. 23:9; Pr 6:16,17; 16:5; Da 4:37; 5:20-24; Mt 23:12; Lu 14:11 Jas 4:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-13","title":"Isaiah 2:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>10:33,34; 14:8; 37:24; Eze 31:3-12; Am 2:5; Zec 11:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-14","title":"Isaiah 2:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>30:25; 40:4; Ps 68:16; 110:5,6; 2Co 10:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-16","title":"Isaiah 2:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the ships. 23:1; 1Ki 10:22; 22:48,49; Ps 47:7; Re 18:17-19 pleasant pictures. Heb. pictures of desire. Nu 33:52; Re 18:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-17","title":"Isaiah 2:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>the loftiness. 11; 13:11; Jer 48:29,30; Eze 28:2-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-18","title":"Isaiah 2:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>the idols. 27:9; Eze 36:25; 37:23; Ho 14:8; Zep 1:3; Zec 13:2 he shall utterly abolish. or, shall utterly pass away.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-19","title":"Isaiah 2:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>And they. 10,21; 1Sa 13:6; 14:11; Jer 16:16; Ho 10:8; Mic 7:17; Lu 23:30 Heb 11:38; Re 6:15; 9:6 earth. Heb. dust. for fear. 10; 2Th 1:9 when he. 30:32; Ps 7:6; 18:6-15; 76:7-9; 114:5-7; Mic 1:3,4; Na 1:3-6 Hab 3:3-14; Hag 2:6,21,22; Heb 12:26; 2Pe 3:10-13; Re 6:12-14 Re 11:13,19; 16:18; 20:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-20","title":"Isaiah 2:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>cast. 30:22; 31:7; 46:1; Ho 14:8; Php 3:7,8 his idols of silver. Heb. the idols of his silver, etc. 46:6 each one for himself to. or, for him to.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-21","title":"Isaiah 2:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>go. 10,19; Ex 33:22; Job 30:6; So 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-2-22","title":"Isaiah 2:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Cease. Ps 62:9; 146:3; Jer 17:5 whose. Ge 2:7; 7:22; Job 27:3 for wherein. Job 7:15-21; Ps 8:4; 144:3,4</p>"}]}